# OCR Service Test Data - Financial Documents .gitignore
#
# This file specifies which financial document files should be excluded from version control
# to prevent repository bloat while ensuring that documentation and configuration files
# are properly tracked. Financial documents are typically large binary files that would
# significantly increase the repository size if included.

# Exclude all binary financial document files by default
*.pdf
*.PDF
*.tiff
*.TIFF
*.tif
*.TIF
*.png
*.PNG
*.jpg
*.JPG
*.jpeg
*.JPEG

# Exclude financial data exports
*.csv
*.CSV
*.xlsx
*.XLSX
*.xls
*.XLS

# Exclude large data files
*.zip
*.ZIP
*.tar.gz
*.TAR.GZ

# Exclude temporary files
*.tmp
*~

# Keep all README files and documentation
!README.md
!README.txt
!*.md

# Keep configuration files
!*.json
!*.yaml
!*.yml
!*.config

# Keep metadata files
!metadata.csv
!financial_document_index.csv
!financial_annotations.csv

# INSTRUCTIONS FOR FINANCIAL TEST DOCUMENTS
#
# The actual financial test documents are not stored in the Git repository to avoid bloat.
# To obtain the financial test documents for development and testing:
#
# 1. Download the financial document test package from the secure S3 bucket:
#    s3://mca-documents-staging/test-data/financial_documents.zip
#
# 2. Extract the package to this directory, preserving the folder structure
#
# 3. Run the verification script to ensure all required financial test documents are present:
#    python ../../../verify_test_data.py typed_documents/financial_documents
#
# 4. The financial documents include various types such as:
#    - Bank statements
#    - Tax returns
#    - Profit and loss statements
#    - Balance sheets
#    - Income statements
#    - Cash flow statements
#    - Credit reports
#
# For more information, see the README.md file in this directory.